[{"client_msg_id":"2d2c194d-9657-4af0-a431-69bec5dc14e4","type":"message","user":"UP6PA1UBE","text":"include は動詞だったりするし。","ts":"1633772040.053900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"XF0"}]},{"client_msg_id":"f1c32ff8-d947-44d4-a9c7-080fd93bfe25","type":"message","user":"UP6PA1UBE","text":"Javascript の `Array.includes()` 的に考えて `includes()` かな","ts":"1633771966.053500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"X3gLs"}]},{"client_msg_id":"a537468f-13ce-4f19-885d-0b7336704917","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"すでに `equals()` とか `exists()` とかが存在している","ts":"1633770266.052800","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"OupG+"}]},{"client_msg_id":"80c73fa0-3aae-4c9a-be99-f3cf8fcf440f","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"ついでにどなたか意見聞きたいんですが、themis.vim に入れるとして、`include()` と `includes()` どっちがいいですかね? ニュアンスの違いがよくわかっていない…","ts":"1633770229.052400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"iPvfd"}]},{"client_msg_id":"3c670136-4dc4-4010-84fd-19c2dac302a8","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"素直に既存のやつに習って実装しよ…","ts":"1633769897.051300","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"otz","count":1,"users":["UAZ33BKV2"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"UXJ"}]},{"client_msg_id":"b82ca207-d058-432d-9630-de23ee8aeb21","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"まあでも、例えば themis.vim にこのヘルパを入れるにあたって、「右側が配列だった場合は↑のようなチェックに切り替わる。配列じゃない場合は普通に要素があるかチェックする。配列が含まれているか確認したい場合は `[ary]` とする」みたいな仕様にすることは可能ではあるけど、単に罠が増えるだけで嬉しい人はいないよなw","ts":"1633769872.051000","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"5En"}]},{"client_msg_id":"c8fba468-4da3-4f88-94a3-7e919b37193e","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"(実際にあるのかどうかは知らないw)","ts":"1633769718.049700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"3UZ+"}]},{"client_msg_id":"806e0379-fa09-4bdd-8a75-63b86f4ad068","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"例えば Haskell の場合は文字列は文字通り文字の配列 `[Char]` として定義されているので、仮に include ヘルパ的なのがあるとしたら私の言ってる動作になるはずなんですよね","ts":"1633769699.049500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"Z3q"}]},{"client_msg_id":"d1a044ef-30e5-424c-a5c6-2b86353e83c0","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"いい悪いは別にすると、オブジェクト指向的な場合なら arry.include(hoge) とstr.include(hoge) と考えると、まあアリだけど、データ列に対してなのか、集合に対してなのかと考えるとナイですなあ","ts":"1633769586.048100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"cy6cy"}]},{"client_msg_id":"fbae75ea-7e2c-439e-916e-49e7c5b732fc","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"この include のやつ、文字列の場合は部分文字列を探すけど、配列の場合は要素を探す。利便性とかを考えると正しいとは思うんだけど、どうも一貫性がないような気もしてしまう。\nどういうことかと言うと、 `include('abcde', 'bcd')` とあったら、`abcde` は `bcd` の並びを含んでいるので true になる。\nでは `include(['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e'], ['b', 'c', 'd'])` はどうかと言うと、左の配列は `['b', 'c', 'd']` と言う配列を要素に含んでいないので false になる。\n実際問題として「配列の一部の並びを含んでいるかどうか」なんてのをチェックしたいシーンはそうそうない。ないんだが…一貫性が気になってしまうw","ts":"1633769477.046300","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"naruhodo","count":1,"users":["UL6CFN8NR"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"1otdY"}]}]
